s+='\n## 8. Short stochastic experiment (finite evidence only)\n\n'
s+='simulate.py implements the exact uniformized continuous-time process on a 24-by-24 periodic square. Independent potential updates at every site have rate R=max(beta_1+delta_1,beta_2+delta_2). An occupied source of type i dies with probability delta_i/R, attempts a birth with probability beta_i/R (target uniform over four neighbors, accepted only if vacant), and otherwise makes a null update. Empty sources make null updates. Thus every specified death and per-neighbor birth generator rate is reproduced exactly. The global Poisson rate is 576R. Initial states are independent with probabilities (0.1,0.45,0.45). Six replicates per parameter choice use seeds 7007+100*case_id+rep, at times 0,10,30,60. Full trajectories and summary are in simulation.json. The job took about 16 seconds and used arrays of 576 sites, far below 1 GB.\n\n'
s+='| (beta_1,delta_1; beta_2,delta_2) | ratios | mean rho_1(60) | mean rho_2(60) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n'
o=json.loads(Path('simulation.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
for a in o['cases']:
 last=a['summary'][-1];s+=f"| ({a['beta1']},{a['delta1']}; {a['beta2']},{a['delta2']}) | {a['ratio1']:.4g}>{a['ratio2']:.4g} | {last['rho1_mean']:.6f} | {last['rho2_mean']:.6f} |\n"
s+='\nThe third case has mean rho_1(10)=0.070602 versus rho_2(10)=0.265336 despite the favorable ratio. At least one finite replicate loses type 1. Neither a transient density disadvantage nor finite extinction refutes the infinite-volume conjecture. The other cases also leave substantial type-2 density at time 60, so the experiment cannot certify asymptotic exclusion. No finite-size extrapolation, significance assertion or infinite-volume conclusion is made.\n'
s+='\n## Final assessment\n\nVERDICT: PARTIAL. The source is verified and no exact-match published solution was located in the successful bounded searches. The nearest-neighbor extinction bound, mean-field result, coupling reduction, algebraic identities, and explicit failed intermediate inequality are proved with their scopes above. The central two-supercritical-species case with only ratio ordering and unequal deaths remains unresolved. This is the limit of this attempt; no claim of a complete solution is made.\n'
